# ── TEST FILES ARE NOT ENDPOINTS (2026-09-05) ────────────────────────────
# 36 *.test.js files under api/ were being DEPLOYED as publicly invocable
# serverless functions. Vercel filesystem-routes api/, and a LEADING UNDERSCORE
# on a directory is the only thing that opts a file out -- which is exactly why
# api/_lib/ (102 test files) and api/_resources/ (1) were never exposed while
# these were.
#
# COUNT CORRECTED BEFORE IT SHIPPED: the first pass said 25, the top-level ones.
# api/sairncash/ (3) and api/sairndental/ (8) carry no underscore either, so
# they route the same way. Probed rather than reasoned about:
#   GET /api/sd-data-approvals.test        -> 500   (top level)
#   GET /api/sairndental/public-book.test  -> 500   (subdirectory, also routed)
#   GET /api/sairncash/verify.test         -> 500   (subdirectory, also routed)
#   GET /api/_lib/auth.test                -> 404   (underscore, correctly hidden)
#
# THE 500 IS THE PROOF, NOT THE PROBLEM. A 500 means Vercel routed the request,
# loaded the module and ran it. The runtime log for one such anonymous GET
# carries the whole suite's output, all 23 assertions; the file `require`s
# api/sd-data.js and executes at module load.
#
# The response body disclosed nothing, so this was never a data leak. It was 36
# anonymous code-execution and compute surfaces existing purely by accident of
# naming -- including api/sairncash/stripe-webhook.test.js.
#
# The pattern is deliberately not scoped to api/: nothing outside a test runner
# ever needs a *.test.js on the server, and one rule is simpler than two.
# Verified before writing it: no non-test file anywhere in the repo requires
# one.
*.test.js

*.DAT*
*.LOG*
*.TM.blf
*.regtrans-ms
AppData/
OneDrive/
Desktop/
Documents/
Downloads/
Music/
Pictures/
Videos/
Contacts/
Favorites/
Links/
Searches/
.config/
.claude/
.bash_history
.gitconfig
.lesshst

# NOTE, 2026-09-05: everything from `*.DAT*` down to `.lesshst` above is
# RESIDUE from when C:\Users\marsh\ was itself a working-tree checkout of this
# repo (see the open-work index rows on that). None of those paths exist in a
# real clone. They are left in place rather than deleted because removing them
# is a deployment-config change with nothing to verify it against, and they
# cost nothing where they are -- but do not read them as evidence that this
# repo has a Documents/ or AppData/ directory. It does not.
